":2,"created_at":"2025-05-11T03:31:49Z","updated_at":"2025-05-20T16:39:47Z","closed_at":"2025-05-20T16:39:45Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: v4.5.dev3.official [55fc6e73f] and v4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6]\n- Not reproducible in v4.3.stable.official [77dcf97d8]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.dev3 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 3 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce GTX 750 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7247) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-6400 CPU @ 2.70GHz (4 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen searching for a file on the FileSystem, selecting it, searching for another one completely different, selecting that one, then going back to the first search and dragging that file, it'll grab 2 files instead.\n\nI couldn't replicate but sometimes doing something similar to this instead of grabbing the right file it would grab the previously searched for file. I hope the issues are related, if I manage to replicate I'll make a separate report.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSearch for a file, select it, search for a different named file, so that the first selected file doesn't appear, select that one. Search again for the first file, drag and drop that first file. Both files are grabbed instead.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ef532137-5806-47c4-abaf-9b1ac5cd476c\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nNone needed.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"